title: Moves and candidates
tags: [[Reconcile]]
kind: reference
summary: How reconcile decides a moved file — a definitive match is followed, a strong or weak one only offered — step by step.

A whole-repository reconcile, step by step:

''1.'' Splits the metarecords with a position into ''active'' (the path exists) and ''orphaned'' (a stale path).

''2.'' Walks the disk, collecting every eligible path.

''3. Fingerprint phase'' — for each orphan, among the unmatched paths on disk:

|!Evidence |!Verdict |
|same size, same partial hash, same full hash |''definitive'': `mfr_path` follows the file and its `mfr_*` fields are refreshed — counted as `moved` |
|same size, same partial hash, no full hash stored |''strong candidate'' — offered |
|same size, no partial hash stored |''weak candidate'' — offered |
|different size or partial hash |no match |
|no size stored |the orphan is skipped: nothing to go on |

''4. Similarity phase'', only with a threshold — the still-unmatched orphans and new paths scored on names and sizes ([[File similarity]]);

''5. Create'' — new paths claimed by nothing get their metarecord (with missing parent directories); a path that is some orphan's candidate is ''not'' created, it waits for your decision;

''6.'' Orphans matched by nothing keep their stale path, untouched — reconcile never sets `mfr_path` to `nothing`;

''7. Refresh'' the stat fields of what is in place (only changed fields are written, so an idle reconcile adds nothing to the log; hashes are left alone), then the ''MIME'' and ''metadata'' phases for files lacking them.

All of it is one transaction, one revision. Offline mount points are pruned from the walk
and from the orphan split: their existence on disk is unknown, not false.

A candidate in the result:

```
{"metarecord_uuid": "abc…", "stale_path": "/music/jazz/old.mp3",
 "matches": [{"path": "/music2/jazz_copy.mp3", "fingerprint": "partial_hash"},
             {"path": "/backup/unknown.mp3", "fingerprint": "size"},
             {"path": "/archive/old_renamed.mp3", "fingerprint": "similarity", "score": 0.82}]}
```

Confirm one by writing the orphan's `mfr_path` (forced); until then it is offered again.
Directories are matched by path only, so a moved directory is an orphan with, at best,
a similarity candidate. Following orphans by content outside a reconcile:
`mf orphan relink`.
